# Since 2026-10-30 the deploy context is NOT the repository: scripts/deploy.sh
# assembles it in /tmp/kestrel-studio-deploy from a whitelist (public/,
# .build/linux-x86_64/kestrel-studio, Dockerfile, docker-compose.yml,
# .dockerignore, Makefile). Everything the image needs is already built on the
# dev machine, because the host's outbound bandwidth (~65 KB/s) makes installing
# or compiling there impractical. node_modules and dist used to be shipped by the
# Node pipeline and are gone with it.
#
# So the list below only bites on a manual `docker compose build` from a full
# checkout. It must keep excluding runtime state (data/, storage/) and secrets
# (.env), and must NOT exclude public/ or .build/ — those are the inputs.
#
# Every path below is anchored with a leading slash. Unanchored patterns match
# at ANY depth, and a bare `storage` silently deleted
# node_modules/.pnpm/multer@2.4.0/node_modules/multer/storage, which surfaced as
# `Cannot find module './storage/disk'` at runtime. Keep the slashes.
/data
/storage
/.git
/.gitignore
/docs
/nest/server/__tests__
/nest/client/__tests__
/.claude
/.env
*.log
